@startuml
title CycleFar — Change future training

autonumber
hide footbox

actor Rider
boundary "Owner-scoped\nchange controller" as Controller
control "Planning change service" as ChangeService
control "FuturePrescriber" as Prescriber
control "ExistingPlanConfiguration" as ExistingConfiguration
control "PlanBuilder" as Builder
control "HorizonMaterializer" as Materializer
control "LoadContext, WeeklyLoadCap\nand LoadReduction" as LoadRules
database "PostgreSQL" as Database

note over ChangeService
  Entry service: AvailabilityChanger, TimeOffPlanner
  or MissedWorkoutResolver, according to rider action.
end note

Rider -> Controller: submit change to an owned plan/workout
Controller -> Database: resolve rider-owned plan/workout
Controller -> ChangeService: apply change
group transaction under plan lock
  ChangeService -> Database: lock owned plan
  alt change availability
    ChangeService -> Database: version availability template and slots
    ChangeService -> ChangeService: choose one-week or from-date range
  else add or remove time off
    ChangeService -> Database: save or remove time-off period
    ChangeService -> ChangeService: group future dates by effective template
  else replan after a missed workout
    ChangeService -> Database: retain source as missed
    ChangeService -> ChangeService: choose today..day 13, bounded by plan end\nuse today's effective template
  end

  loop each affected range and its selected availability slots
    ChangeService -> Prescriber: replace!(dates, selected slots)
    Prescriber -> Database: lock plan
    Prescriber -> Prescriber: restrict replacement dates to today onward inside plan
    Prescriber -> Database: read pre-break levels and time-off context
    Prescriber -> Database: remove replaceable planned regular workouts\nand blocked-date planned specials
    Prescriber -> ExistingConfiguration: build from saved plan and supplied slots
    ExistingConfiguration --> Prescriber: saved plan and slots; assessment exclusions for time off/return ramps
    Prescriber -> Builder: preview(configuration)
    Builder -> Builder: align recovery; rank unblocked FTP-test dates\nforecast prescriptions and metrics
    Builder -> LoadRules: apply ordered cap reductions to forecasts
    Builder -> Builder: budget taper stages against comparable peak load\nretain event/opener and save reduced main-set factors
    Builder --> Prescriber: deterministic prescriptions and generation choices
    Prescriber -> Prescriber: skip blocked dates; apply return-ramp/resumption rules
    Prescriber -> Database: create outlines on empty dates\nretain target/filler choices, taper factors, ceilings and effective levels
    Prescriber -> Materializer: call(plan)
    Materializer -> Database: lock plan; read eligible outlines and fixed workouts
    Materializer -> Materializer: apply accepted bias once; generate actual profiles/metrics
    Materializer -> LoadRules: recheck actual load against comparable hard week
    LoadRules --> Materializer: bounded definitions or infeasible-load warning
    Materializer -> Database: save new canonical steps, profiles and load references
  end
end
ChangeService --> Controller: change applied
Controller --> Rider: redirect to calendar

note over Prescriber, Database
  Only future planned records in affected dates are replaceable.
  Completed/missed workouts, plan phases and event date remain fixed.
  Missed Leave and Move do not enter this re-prescription flow;
  ordinary and missed Move use Workouts::Mover and shared destination rules.
  Normal hard-week duration and specific subtype intent remain fixed.
  Taper duration follows stage budgets; saved work factors preserve power bands.
  Only affected dates are replaced; existing plans are not bulk rewritten.
  Calendar review shows a warning when valid load reductions are exhausted.
end note
@enduml
